its a wrong assumption. `find` is designed to make a simple queries and `QueryBuilder` is designed to make more complex queries. If you don't like QueryBuilder I would like to suggest you to like it because to feel all benefits of it.

>  "We want all users with at least one post".

how do you do it with `find` right now? In `next` where expressions automatically create inner joins, e.g.

```ts
find(User, {
  where: {
      post: {
           id: 1
      }
  }
})
```

will create `SELECT * FROM user INNER JOIN post WHERE post.id=1`

